Module 1: Auth & User Management (Login, Registration, Password Reset, Roles & Permissions, Audit Logging)
Setup: Repository Protection, PR/Issue Templates, Work Agreements, & DB Seeding

SECTION 2: SPRINT 1 BOARD USER STORIES & ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

User Authentication & Role Access
Title: User Authentication & Role Access
As a system user, I want to log in securely so that I can access features authorized for my specific role.

Acceptance Criteria:
User can log in with valid credentials and receive appropriate session/token.
System displays clear error messages for invalid credentials without revealing specific sensitive details.
Unauthenticated users are redirected to the login page when attempting to access protected routes.
Role-based permission checks are enforced on protected UI views and API endpoints.

Audit Logging System
Title: User Action Audit Logger
As an Administrator, I want key actions logged automatically so that I can audit user activities across the system.

Acceptance Criteria:
The system records audit_user() details into the audit_log table upon key actions.
Audit records capture user ID, action type, timestamp, target entity, and IP/session context.
Database triggers/functions execute cleanly without breaking or slowing valid business transactions.

Sprint Board & Backlog Setup
Title: Sprint Board & Roadmap Mapping
As a Scrum Master, I want all user stories defined and mapped so that the development team can execute Sprint 1 effectively.

Acceptance Criteria:
All Sprint 1 backlog items are published on the project board with clear titles and descriptions.
Every Sprint 1 story includes defined, testable Acceptance Criteria.
The 6-module roadmap spanning the 8-week limit is documented and communicated to the team.

SECTION 3: DEFINITION OF DONE (SCRUM MASTER CHECKLIST)

